control: Write-backs, reloads, re-reads and the re-seal take turns under one lock of the connections, so the process's own writes each land and none is read back as someone else's
removes: a write-back no longer takes the connections' lock, so one whose compare-and-set waits behind another's reads the other's bytes back as someone else's and its rotation is lost
packages: ./process/connections
tests: TestTwoEndsWhoseWritesInterleaveBothLand
scheduled-count: no
integration: yes

